; better-sqlite3 ships prebuilt native binaries per OS/CPU (via N-API,
; which is stable across Node.js versions), but its package still
; defines a binding.gyp file, which makes npm attempt a from-source
; rebuild by default on every install — unnecessary, slower, and it
; can fail on machines without a C/C++ build toolchain even though a
; working prebuild is already bundled. This skips that rebuild and
; uses the bundled prebuild directly. None of this project's other
; dependencies need install/postinstall scripts, so this is safe.
ignore-scripts=true
